\f0\b\fs96 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Capability negotiation\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices \cf2 ACP uses\'a0
\f0\b capability negotiation
\f1\b0 \'a0so agents and sellers can discover what each supports and agree on a common set of features for a checkout. A single\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 \'a0object is sent in requests (from the agent) and returned in responses (from the seller), with the seller returning only the\'a0
\f0\b intersection
\f1\b0 \'a0of mutually supported capabilities.\

\f0\b\fs64 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Why capability negotiation?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices \cf2 Agents and sellers can support different payment methods, authentication flows, and interaction patterns. Without a standard way to negotiate:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Agents cannot know in advance whether they can complete a given checkout.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Sellers cannot communicate requirements (e.g., 3D Secure for certain transactions).\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 New features (e.g., biometric auth, BNPL) require ad-hoc integration instead of a single, extensible mechanism.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Capability negotiation addresses this by:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Single capability declaration
\f1\b0 \'a0\'97 The same\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0structure is used for both parties; context (request vs response) indicates who is declaring.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Intersection-based response
\f1\b0 \'a0\'97 The seller returns only the intersection of supported capabilities, so the agent does not need to compute compatibility.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Early incompatibility detection
\f1\b0 \'a0\'97 Mismatches can be detected before payment, with clear errors or fallbacks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs64 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Where capabilities appear\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs24 \AppleTypeServices \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Requests:
\f1\b0 \'a0Agents MUST include\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0on checkout session create requests. At minimum, agents declare intervention support, e.g.\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 \{"interventions": \{"supported": []\}\}
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 .\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Responses:
\f1\b0 \'a0Sellers MUST include\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0on all checkout session responses (create, retrieve, update, complete). The response holds the negotiated capabilities for that session.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 \'a0in requests is write-only and is not echoed back; the response always reflects the seller-computed negotiated capabilities.\

\f0\b\fs64 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The capabilities object\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs52 \AppleTypeServices \cf6 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 Agent request (what the agent sends)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Agents declare what they can handle, especially for user interventions (e.g., 3DS, biometric, address verification):\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 interventions
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0(optional but recommended):\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 supported
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97 Array of intervention types the agent can handle, such as\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 3ds
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0or\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 biometric
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 .\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 display_context
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97 How the agent presents interventions:\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 native
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0within an application, a browser\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 webview
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 , etc.\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 redirect_context
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97 How redirects are handled:\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 in_app
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 ,\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 external_browser
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 , or\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 none
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 .\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 max_redirects
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97 Maximum number of redirects the agent can handle in one flow.\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 max_interaction_depth
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97 Maximum depth of nested interactions (e.g., 3DS inside a webview).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Agents may also declare\'a0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 extensions
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 \'a0they understand (e.g.,\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 ["discount"]
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ) so the seller can enable compatible\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.agenticcommerce.dev/docs/concepts/extensions"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \strokec2 extensions}}\'a0for the session.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs52 \cf6 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 Seller response (negotiated capabilities)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 The seller returns only what both sides support and adds seller-specific information:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 payment
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97 Payment configuration for this session. Includes\'a0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 handlers
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 : the list of payment handlers (e.g., tokenized card, wallet) the seller accepts. Each handler describes its name, version, spec URL, whether it uses Delegate Payment, PCI requirements, and instrument schemas.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 interventions
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 :\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 supported
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97\'a0
\f0\b Intersection
\f1\b0 \'a0of agent and seller supported interventions. Only intervention types both support appear here.\
\ls5\ilvl1
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 required
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97 (Optional) Interventions the seller requires for this session (e.g.,\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 ["3ds"]
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 ). If empty or absent, none are required.\
\ls5\ilvl1
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 enforcement
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97 (Optional) When required interventions apply:\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 always
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 ,\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 conditional
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0(e.g., based on risk), or\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 optional
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 extensions
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0\'97 For sessions with\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.agenticcommerce.dev/docs/concepts/extensions"}}{\fldrslt extensions}}, the seller returns an array of\'a0
\f0\b extension declarations
\f1\b0 \'a0(name, schema/spec URLs, which schema fields they extend) for extensions active in this session.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Note:\'a0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 interventions.supported
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 \'a0in the response is exactly the intersection of supported interventions.
\f1\b0 \'a0The agent does not need to compute it; the seller does and returns only mutually supported values.\

\f0\b\fs64 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Intersection semantics\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices \cf2 When the agent sends\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities.interventions.supported
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , the seller:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Computes the intersection with its own supported interventions.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Returns that intersection in\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities.interventions.supported
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0in the response.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Adds seller-only fields (
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 required
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 ,\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 enforcement
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 ) and payment/extensions as applicable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Example:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Agent sends:\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 \{"interventions": \{"supported": ["3ds", "biometric", "address_verification"]\}\}
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Seller internally supports:\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 ["3ds", "address_verification"]
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Seller returns:\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 \{"interventions": \{"supported": ["3ds", "address_verification"], "required": [], "enforcement": "conditional"\}\}
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 So the agent immediately sees that for this session only 3DS and address verification are mutually supported; biometric is not.\

\f0\b\fs64 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Intervention compatibility\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices \cf2 A session is compatible for interventions when:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 The intersection (returned in\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 supported
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 ) includes every intervention in\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 required
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 ,\'a0
\f0\b or
\f1\b0 \'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 required
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0is empty/absent, and\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Any expected interaction depth does not exceed the agent\'92s declared\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 max_interaction_depth
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0(if present).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 If the seller requires 3DS but the agent declared\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 supported: []
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , the intersection is empty. The seller still returns\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 \'a0(e.g.\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 supported: []
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ,\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 required: ["3ds"]
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ) and can add an error message (e.g. with code\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 intervention_required
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ) so the agent can inform the user that 3DS is required but not supported in the current environment.\

\f0\b\fs64 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Payment and extensions\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\fs24 \AppleTypeServices \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Payment:
\f1\b0 \'a0The seller advertises payment handlers in\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities.payment.handlers
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 . Each handler identifies how payment is processed (e.g., tokenized card via Delegate Payment), which PSP is used, and which instrument schemas apply. The agent uses this to know which payment methods and flows are available for the session.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Extensions:
\f1\b0 \'a0The agent can list extension identifiers it understands in\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities.extensions
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0in the request. The seller returns\'a0
\fs28 \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 capabilities.extensions
\fs24 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec5 \'a0in the response as an array of\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.agenticcommerce.dev/docs/concepts/extensions"}}{\fldrslt extension declaration}}\'a0objects (name, extends, schema, spec) for extensions active in that session. This allows optional, composable features (e.g.,\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.agenticcommerce.dev/docs/concepts/extensions"}}{\fldrslt discounts}}) without changing the core schema.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs64 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
